 "result_text": "`bytes_sql_quote()` in `src/DocumentTemplate/DT_Var.py` now returns text instead of bytes on Python 3. The quoted value can therefore be concatenated with the rest of the SQL query string, which is what `<dtml-sqlvar xy type=\"string\">` needs. I haven't run the tests or tried it with a real template.\n\nIt decodes the quoted bytes as UTF-8, as in the patch from the issue. Bytes that aren't valid UTF-8 will now raise a `UnicodeDecodeError`.\n\nOn Python 2 it still returns the quoted value unchanged. There `bytes` is `str`, so decoding would turn it into `unicode`, which I assumed you didn't want.",
